To support multiple Telegram Bot API libraries, such as `python-telegram-bot`, `pyrogram`, and `aiogram`, you can use an abstract base class (ABC) to define the interface that each library must implement. This will allow you to write your code against the interface, rather than a specific library, and switch between libraries simply by changing the implementation of the ABC.

Here's a basic example of an ABC for the Telegram Bot API:
```python
from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class TelegramBotAPI(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def send_message(self, chat_id, text):
        pass

    @abstractmethod
    def send_photo(self, chat_id, photo):
        pass

    # ... other methods ...

class PythonTelegramBotAPI(TelegramBotAPI):
    def __init__(self, token):
        import telegram
        self.bot = telegram.Bot(token=token)

    def send_message(self, chat_id, text):
        self.bot.send_message(chat_id=chat_id, text=text)

    def send_photo(self, chat_id, photo):
        self.bot.send_photo(chat_id=chat_id, photo=photo)

    # ... other methods ...

class PyrogramAPI(TelegramBotAPI):
    def __init__(self, token):
        import pyrogram
        self.client = pyrogram.Client(token=token)

    def send_message(self, chat_id, text):
        self.client.send_message(chat_id=chat_id, text=text)

    def send_photo(self, chat_id, photo):
        self.client.send_photo(chat_id=chat_id, photo=photo)

    # ... other methods ...

class AiogramAPI(TelegramBotAPI):
    def __init__(self, token):
        import aiogram.bot
        self.bot = aiogram.bot.Bot(token=token)

    async def send_message(self, chat_id, text):
        await self.bot.send_message(chat_id=chat_id, text=text)

    async def send_photo(self, chat_id, photo):
        await self.bot.send_photo(chat_id=chat_id, photo=photo)

    # ... other methods ...
```
In this example, the `TelegramBotAPI` ABC defines the interface that each library must implement, and the concrete classes, such as `PythonTelegramBotAPI`, `PyrogramAPI`, and `AiogramAPI`, provide the implementation for each library.

The `TelegramBot` class can use an instance of the API implementation, such as `PythonTelegramBotAPI`, `PyrogramAPI`, or `AiogramAPI`, to send messages and perform other actions:
```python
import logging

class TelegramBot:
    def __init__(self, token, api_class=PythonTelegramBotAPI, plugins=None, log_level=logging.INFO):
        self.token = token
        self.api = api_class(token)
        self.plugins = plugins or []
        self.commands = []
        self.users = {}
        self.events = []
        self.logger = logging.
```

