    return 0;
}
```
This will output the string "Hello, World!" to the console, followed by a newline character.

It's worth noting that the `std::cout` is a stream object that is connected to the console's output, and the `<<` operator is used to send data to the stream. The `std::endl` is used to insert a newline character and flush the stream.

Keep in mind that while MASM can be used to write low-level system code, it's not the best option when you want to write high-level, portable code. C++ is a high-level programming language that provides a rich set of libraries that can be used to perform a wide range of tasks, including input/output operations.

