Defining multiple subpasses in a Vulkan render pass involves creating multiple instances of the `VkSubpassDescription` struct and adding them to the `pSubpasses` array of the `VkRenderPassCreateInfo` struct. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. Create an array of `VkAttachmentReference` structs, one for each color attachment and depth/stencil attachment that you plan to use in your render pass. These structs will define the layout and format of each attachment.
2. Create an array of `VkSubpassDescription` structs, one for each subpass that you want to define in your render pass. Each `VkSubpassDescription` struct should specify the color and depth/stencil attachments that will be used in the subpass, as well as any dependencies that the subpass has on other subpasses.
3. Create a `VkRenderPassCreateInfo` struct and set its `sType`, `pNext`, `flags`, `attachmentCount`, `pAttachments`, `subpassCount`, and `pSubpasses` fields. The `pAttachments` field should be set to the array of `VkAttachmentDescription` structs that describe the properties of each attachment used in the render pass.
4. Call `vkCreateRenderPass()` to create the render pass object.

Here's an example of how to define two subpasses in a render pass, where the second subpass uses the output of the first subpass as input:
```c++
VkAttachmentReference colorAttachmentRef = {
    0, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL
};

VkAttachmentReference depthAttachmentRef = {
    1, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL
};

VkSubpassDescription subpasses[2] = {};

// First subpass - output to color attachment
subpasses[0].pipelineBindPoint = VK_PIPELINE_BIND_POINT_GRAPHICS;
subpasses[0].colorAttachmentCount = 1;
subpasses[0].pColorAttachments = &colorAttachmentRef;
subpasses[0].pDepthStencilAttachment = &depthAttachmentRef;

// Second subpass - input from color attachment
subpasses[1].pipelineBindPoint = VK_PIPELINE_BIND_POINT_GRAPHICS;
subpasses[1].colorAttachmentCount = 1;
subpasses[1].pColorAttachments = &colorAttachmentRef;
subpasses[1].pDepthStencilAttachment = &depthAttachmentRef;
subpasses[1].inputAttachmentCount = 1;
subpasses[1].pInputAttachments = &colorAttachmentRef;

VkAttachmentDescription attachments[2] = {};

// Color attachment
attachments[0].format = VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM;
attachments[0].samples = VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT;
attachments[0].loadOp = VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_CLEAR;
attachments[0].storeOp = VK_ATTACHMENT_STORE_OP_STORE;
attachments[0].stencilLoadOp = VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_DONT_CARE;
attachments[0].stencilStoreOp = VK_ATTACHMENT_STORE_OP_DONT_CARE;
attachments[0].initialLayout = VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED;
attachments[0].finalLayout = VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL;

// Depth/stencil attachment
attachments[1].format = VK_FORMAT_D32_SFLOAT;
