The first enum value is "Unset", which has a value of 0. The other values are defined using the bitwise left shift operator `<<`, which shifts the binary representation of the number 1 a certain number of places to the left. For example, `(1 << 1)` is equivalent to the binary value 10, which is equal to the decimal value 2. Similarly, `(1 << 2)` is equivalent to the binary value 100, which is equal to the decimal value 4.

