fn call_me(num: Option<u32>) {
    for i in 0..num.unwrap_or(5) {
        println!("Ring! Call number {}", i + 1);
    }
}
```
In this example, the `num` parameter is an `Option<u32>` type, which means it can be either `Some(value)` or `None`. Inside the `for` loop, we use the `unwrap_or` method to get the value of `num` if it is `Some(value)`, or a default value of `5` if it is `None`.

