Calculating the number of connected components in a control flow graph (CFG) using Clang Static Analyzer requires working with Clang's CFG representation. Here's an example implementation of a Clang Static Analyzer checker that counts the number of connected components in the CFG of a function. Note that this example only considers the number of connected components in the function's CFG and not the entire program.

First, create a header file named "ConnectedComponentsChecker.h":
```cpp
