To handle conflicts when multiple users edit the same text field in the form, you can use DynamoDB's conditional update feature. You'll need to store a version number for the form in the database, and each time the form is updated, you'll increment the version number. When a user submits an update to the form, you'll include the current version number with the update request. The update will only be applied if the version number in the request matches the version number in the database. If the version numbers don't match, it means that another user has updated the form in the meantime, and the update request will fail. You can then fetch the latest version of the form from the database and merge the conflicting changes.

Here's an updated example of the back-end code that includes conflict handling:
```typescript
import { Controller, Get, Put, Body, ConflictException } from '@nestjs/common';
import { DocumentClient } from 'aws-sdk/clients/dynamodb';
import { AWS_REGION, DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME } from './constants';

@Controller()
export class FormController {
  private readonly dynamoDbClient: DocumentClient;

  constructor() {
    this.dynamoDbClient = new DocumentClient({ region: AWS_REGION });
  }

  @Get('/form')
  async getForm(): Promise<any> {
    const params = {
      TableName: DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME,
      Key: { id: 'form' },
    };
    const data = await this.dynamoDbClient.get(params).promise();
    return data.Item;
  }

  @Put('/form')
  async updateForm(@Body() form: any): Promise<any> {
    const getParams = {
      TableName: DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME,
      Key: { id: 'form' },
    };
    const getData = await this.dynamoDbClient.get(getParams).promise();
    const currentVersion = getData.Item.version;

    const updateParams = {
      TableName: DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME,
      Key: { id: 'form' },
      UpdateExpression:
        'set #name = :name, #email = :email, #phone = :phone, #version = :newVersion',
      ExpressionAttributeNames: {
        '#name': 'name',
        '#email': 'email',
        '#phone': 'phone',
        '#version': 'version',
      },
      ExpressionAttributeValues: {
        ':name': form.name,
        ':email': form.email,
        ':phone': form.phone,
        ':newVersion': currentVersion + 1,
      },
      ConditionExpression: '#version = :version',
      ExpressionAttributeValues: {
        ':version': form.version,
      },
      ReturnValues: 'ALL_NEW',
    };

    try {
      const data = await this.dynamoDbClient.update(updateParams).promise();
      return data.Attributes;
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.code === 'ConditionalCheckFailedException') {
        throw new ConflictException('Form has been updated by another user. Please refresh the form and try again.');
      }
      throw error;
    }
  }
}
```
In this updated code, the `updateForm` method first fetches the current version number of the form from the database using the `get` method. Then, it constructs an `updateParams` object that includes the new version number (`currentVersion + 1`) and a `ConditionExpression` that checks if the version number in the request matches the current version number in the database. If the version numbers match, the update is applied using the `update` method, and the updated form is returned. If the version numbers don't match, a `ConflictException` is thrown with an error message indicating that the form has been updated by another user.

